whose default schema has no JS types.


4. Trust boundary in the added subsystem
-----------------------------------------

The Agent Skills node returns the text of Markdown skill files to an LLM agent as instructions.
That agent may hold real, side-effecting tools. Therefore:

    ANYONE WHO CAN WRITE INTO A SKILLS DIRECTORY CAN STEER ANY AGENT THIS NODE IS ATTACHED TO.

The node's "Skills Directory" input can be repointed by any flow editor at any directory readable
by the server process. Skill text is never executed as code — it is quoted reference material,
delimited and escaped by the node — but it is still instruction-shaped input to a model. Treat a
skills directory with the same care as you would treat the agent's system prompt.


